1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
ChipQC: organ-on-a-chip image review.
Local tool and retrospective validation.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
3,072 brightfield frames; six cell types.
59 acquisition-date prefixes.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Does a model handle unseen imaging dates?
Scores estimate expert good/bad labels.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,081
Demo dates excluded from training.

5
00:00:22,081 --> 00:00:23,840
230320_47: expert label good.

6
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:31,110
P(good) = 92.3%.
Interface illustration; see study results.

7
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:32,851
230524_24: expert label bad.

8
00:00:32,851 --> 00:00:40,124
P(good) = 7.7%.
Interface illustration; see study results.

9
00:00:40,124 --> 00:00:41,884
230524_73: expert label good.

10
00:00:41,884 --> 00:00:48,936
P(good) = 50.0%: scientist review.

11
00:00:48,936 --> 00:00:55,430
Focus and appearance support review.
They do not establish function or safety.

12
00:00:55,430 --> 00:01:09,430
Five candidates: random image folds
versus dates excluded from training.

13
00:01:09,430 --> 00:01:17,430
MobileNet + logistic regression.
Date-held-out AUC 0.748; random 0.816.

14
00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:26,430
95% date-bootstrap CI: 0.694 to 0.797.
New labs and tissue function untested.

15
00:01:26,430 --> 00:01:34,430
Install pinned dependencies; fetch images.
Compute features and frozen embeddings.

16
00:01:34,430 --> 00:01:43,430
Run evaluation; follow the README.
Start the demo checkpoint; dates held out.

17
00:01:43,430 --> 00:01:49,430
